  "scope_notes": [
    "EditPtOn displays curve Greville points without replacing source geometry or consuming model history. PointsOn switches back to controls; mode switches clear the owner grip picks.",
    "Move and the existing affine grip transforms reconstruct the original degree, knots, control count, parameter domain and weights through the shared original-basis interpolation and exact rational station checks. Curve primitives promote to NURBS only when edited.",
    "The document stages mixed object/grip outputs and Copy, preserving source geometry, selection and Redo when a later grip overflows. Display mode and picks share the existing history exchange policy.",
    "Viewport previews use the same edit operation and cache the grip mode alongside source snapshot, indices, transform, tolerance and density.",
    "Whole-object ScalePositions Copy preserves the source grip mode and picked indices on the copied owner.",
    "The shared portable faer interpolation solver is used for document edit grips in both application build configurations. Native-smlib enablement does not imply a new native grip interpolation path.",
    "Limits: degree at most 17, at most 1000 stored controls, common-sign rational weights, clamped open/closed inputs or periodic inputs with exact repeated tails. Full-order knots retain sided stations.",
    "Smooth rejects selected edit grips. SetPt does not accept grips. SubD editing, closed seam aliases, native ordering, full Rhino behavior and performance remain unqualified.",
    "No new live Rhino captures were obtained; live retesting was deferred because of the recorded Wine SSPI startup issue. Retained native control-grip replays exercise shared code and do not qualify edit-grip behavior."
  ],
